olor of its controller's choice until end of turn. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)", '{4}, {T}: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', '{B}{R}: Each player loses 1 life.', '{G/W}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Hexhunter: Destroy target enchantment.', '{R/G}{R/G}{R/G}: Foxfire Oak gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}{G}: Each blocked creature gets +1/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice a Mountain: Valleymaker deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a Forest: Choose a player. That player adds {G}{G}{G}.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Target creature becomes the color or colors of your choice until end of turn.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B/R}, {T}: Add {B}{B}, {B}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G/W}, {T}: Add {G}{G}, {G}{W}, or {W}{W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R/G}, {T}: Add {R}{R}, {R}{G}, or {G}{G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{U/B}, {T}: Add {U}{U}, {U}{B}, or {B}{B}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W/U}, {T}: Add {W}{W}, {W}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}{C}. Spend this mana only on costs that contain {X}.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\nPut a -1/-1 counter on Devoted Druid: Untap Devoted Druid.', "{T}: Choose any number of target creatures. Each of those creatures gains persist until end of turn. (When it dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nPut a -1/-1 counter on Barrenton Medic: Untap Barrenton Medic.', '{T}: Target player discards a card. Activate only during your turn.\\nPut a -1/-1 counter on Cinderhaze Wretch: Untap Cinderhaze Wretch.', '{U/B}: Loch Korrigan gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{W/U}, {Q}: Look at the top card of your library. You may exile that card. ({Q} is the untap symbol.)', '{W/U}: Parapet Watchers gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{W}, {T}: Remove a -1/-1 counter from target creature. If you do, you gain 2 life.', '{W}, {T}: Target blocking creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{X}, Discard a card with mana value X: Knollspine Invocation deals X damage to any target.', '{X}, {T}: You gain X life.']
flavor: ['"\'Tis a strange creature indeed that chooses the vanquished over the victor."\\n—Awylla, elvish safewright', '"All glamers lifted, all lies revealed, all flesh exposed."\\n—Awylla, elvish safewright', '"All manner of curses, blights, and luckspoils infect Shadowmoor. We stalk them all, one perilous quest at a time."', '"An axe may break upon a ribbon if the ribbon\'s will is the stronger."\\n—Awylla, elvish safewright', '"Are you tired? You look tired."', '"Beware of trees that talk. Their words are threats. And mind the ones that sway and creak. They too threaten us, but in a foreign tongue."\\n—*The Book of Other Folk*', '"Beware the merrows, whose envy and covetousness surpasses even that of the ravenous whirlpools where they dwell."\\n—*The Book of Other Folk*', '"Bits of fallen scarecrow, laces of elfskin leather, teeth of an axeshark merrow . . . An industrious soul can find new uses for the most mundane items."\\n—Mowagh the Gwyllion', '"Boggarts are easy to get around. Just toss some mutton in another direction. Giants are a little harder. You have to be quick to avoid their steps. Cinders are the difficult ones, but even they have fears to be exploited."', '"Did you expect me to dodge? How quaint."\\n—Olka, mistmeadow witch', '"Don\'t look upon still waters without first breaking the surface. The korrigan will catch you with her gaze and drag you to your death."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"Dreams are fleeting. Reality even more so."\\n—Oona, queen of the fae', '"He bears the marks of ages upon his skin, memories of dreams long dead and best left buried."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"He is a ghost that has never known life."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Here did the Extinguisher steal the light from the world. Here will we sacrifice her to bring the Great Rekindling to our people."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', '"Here lies Gond, hero of Safehold Taldwen. May he ever guide our quest."', '"His laugh, a bellowing, deathly din, slices through the heavens, making them bleed."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"I can stab you where it hurts, or where you will feel absolutely nothing."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', '"I doubt that faeries understand how short their lives are, compared to the rest of us. If they did, would they so readily charge into battle, heedless of the danger before them?"\\n—Awylla, elvish safewright', '"I have a gift. The ability to sense encroaching darkness has saved many lives. And yet constantly feeling the force of so much ugliness is a terrible burden."', '"I know one night it won\'t come back. Then I\'ll know it\'s truly done its job."\\n—Braenna, cobblesmith', '"I need a better hiding place."', '"I refuse to die—not at the hands of one such as you."', '"I rigged it together from wicker and scrap, yet somehow I find it unalterably perfect."\\n—Braenna, cobblesmith', '"If you see ghostly lights by the river, eat three twigs of marshroot to ward off kelpies."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"It was vast, a great sheet of soaring wings, and equally silent. It caught us unawares and blocked our view of the kithkin stronghold."\\n—Grensch, merrow cutthroat', '"It\'s not a matter of deserving. It\'s a matter of strength. The power to hold versus the power to take."', '"Life is a circle. Death is a vicious circle."', '"Mana lurks in all things, even in the depths of one\'s own heart."', '"None will concede a place for us in this world. If it is not for us, neither shall it be for them. We rest not until they choke in its cold ashes."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', '"Nothing warms my heart better than a spirit kindled with rage."', '"Of all the things that can be stolen, opportunity is the most valuable."', '"Raven\'s Run has awoken, and ravens will no longer cry in its branches."\\n—Roon Ghastbark', '"Seeing is believing" is a fact the merrows ruthlessly exploit in their dealings with the other residents of Shadowmoor.', '"So now you\'ve seen Glen Elendra. Take a good look. It will be the last thing you\'ll ever see."', '"Some folk these days are too restless to dream the dreams we need. We need to teach them to stop and catch their breath."', '"Some say she hid the sun herself, a desperate act to save it from its ultimate extinction."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Some secrets want to be revealed. They burst through the soil of their own accord."\\n—Dindun of Kulrath Mine', '"Terrible wind. It whipped sparks into our skin, then stoked them even hotter!"\\n—Bowen, Barrenton guardcaptain', '"The bigger they are, the more fun it is to watch them fall flat on their faces."', '"The brethren shall blaze with unnatural fire, and the flame shall consume and purify our rage."\\n—Treefolk catastrophe myth', '"The cinders find strength in suffering, the elves in beauty. But if you make an elf suffer, he gets weaker. I wonder what happens if you make a cinder beautiful?"\\n—Hrugash, leech bonder', '"The dead have it easy. They suffer no more. If breaking their rest helps the living, so be it."\\n—Olka, mistmeadow witch', '"The light of beauty protects our journeys through darkness."', '"Their sharp scales would make good armor, if they\'d just stay dead."\\n—Taeryn, cinder armorkeep', '"These bracers were worn by my father and by his mother before him. Boggart fangs have shattered on them. Cinder flames have withered at their touch. While I wear them, the safehold will not fall."', '"Those who are different are untrustworthy, unpredictable. Put your safety in the hands of your own kind."\\n—Bowen, Barrenton guardcaptain', '"Thought? Deceit? Progress? Now you\'re just making it hungry."\\n—Abral, kithkin alchemist', '"Tsk. You\'d think those nasty merrows would know how to hold their breath."\\n—Olka, mistmeadow witch', '"Unsafe Terrain Ahead—Turn Back"\\n—Sign near the former location of Pyrtagh Cairn', '"Vengeance is the echo of the victim\'s own crime."\\n—Grensch, merrow cutthroat', '"Verdant bloom does exist. It merely hides for its own safety."', '"We will give you the peace you seek, though you may not yet know you seek it."', '"We\'re going to need a bigger gate."\\n—Bowen, Barrenton guardcaptain', '"What is a scar? A sign of courage in the face of danger? A mere trick of flesh? Or a constant reminder of agonizing pain, and the follies of war."\\n—Illulia of Nighthearth', '"What she saw crawling upon this world repulsed her. Yet she could not tear her gaze away."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Why allow the fires of others to burn, when ours do not? Why leave them content, while we suffer? If there is to be misery, let it be borne by all."', '"Why enchant feathers to make them sturdy when we can enchant shields to make them fly?"\\n—Braenna, cobblesmith', '"Your seared flesh will be the first step in your journey to dark enlightenment."', "A Bloodwort's blade is salted with blood and peppered with rust, seasoning and slaughtering in a single swipe.", 'A chain of lies as strong as steel.', 'A clique can cause far more mischief than one faerie on its own.', 'A deflated sigh breathed into the horn emerges as an inspiring melody.', 'A delicate veil of glamers can prove as sturdy as iron.', 'A kithkin doun is not so much a town as a fortress, built to withstand the constantly besieging darkness. Only those most watchful and trustworthy are tasked with guarding its walls.', "A kithkin's worst enemy is solitude.", 'A taut slipknot trigger is the only thing standing between you and standing.', "Accept one favor from an ouphe, and you're doomed to accept another.", 'After his hands had crumbled away, leaving only wickedly sharp points, he decided his only purpose was war.', 'All faeries delve for dreams. But not all wait for their victims to fall asleep.', 'Any being that harms them quickly learns its lesson.', 'Any kithkin smith would love to catch a dieflyn for her kiln, relieving her of ever having to gather fuel again.', 'As it wandered Shadowmoor, it did not remember its crime—only its shame.', 'Awylla tried hard to forget the horrors she had seen, but someone else had developed a keen interest in them.', "Before a raid, the members of Wort's gang egg each other on with tales of their hunger and what they'll do to sate it, each outdoing the last.", 'Beware a scarecrow bearing gifts—especially sloshing vessels of acid.', 'Boggarts divide the world into two categories: things you can eat, and things you have to chase down and pummel before you can eat.', 'Built to shuttle goods from the river, it took off one day carrying a cauldron of dyes.', "Cinder beliefs revolve around the Path of Sorrow, a spiritual descent into oblivion. They don't mind taking others on their journey down.", 'Cinder mages enjoy seeing their victims in the throes of bloodlust—and seeing the regret that inevitably follows.', 'Cinder mystics set traps for sluaghs and other spirits of flame, seeking to extract the secrets of the fire their own hearts have lost.', "Cinder pyromancers measure their success by counting their enemies' smoking holes.", 'Cinders carry an ancestral grudge that makes them slow to trust and quick to retaliate.', 'Clear out the cell. Bring in the next prisoner.', 'Dawnglove bloom is a potent nostrum, but the dawnglow brewed from its sap is nothing less than life itself.', 'Death stings the victim only once, but those left behind feel the pain of loss with every passing memory.', "Despite its darkness, Shadowmoor doesn't want for growth. Legions of creeping things thrive in the shade.", 'Do not disturb.', 'Does it reflect the future that once was or the past that can never be?', "Don't stand in his way, for his way is full of pointy things and fire.", 'Doyo suspected the boggarts of brewing a plot against his crop, so he scythed away his grain to clear the sightlines.', 'Dreams of dark nights to come are said to stir in the minds of scheming hollowsages.', 'Driven by their paranoia, kithkin inflict on their foes all the agonies they believe would have been inflicted on them.', 'Each night that his bowl fills, a village mourns.', 'Each night, gloomwidows cull fresh prey for their ravenous hatchlings.', 'Elves search for sources of beauty in a nighted world. Meanwhile, the nighted world searches for the blood of elves.', "Elvish dawnhands test a relic's worthiness before collecting it for the safehold. If it can't stand up to a stiff breeze, it's left behind.", 'Elvish healers carry vials of the balm known as dawnglow, reserving it for those wounds that herbs cannot treat.', 'Every elf in Shadowmoor is charged from birth with a terrible duty: to strike back against the ugliness and darkness, even though they are all around and seemingly without end.', 'Every life ends, but life itself never does.', "For a moment, objects of pure mana glimmered in the wonderstruck boggart's hands. In the next moment, they were in his mouth, as he chewed contentedly.", 'For the Scuzzback gang, it\'s always "raid o\'clock."', 'Giants sleep soundly and long, sometimes for long enough that a crust of earth and moss grows over them. But inevitably something disturbs their slumber, and they wake unhappy.', "Gloomwidow venom is particularly virulent during the spider's first years, when it does most of its hunting near the forest floor.", "Grimeblotters spend so much time in the Dark Meanders that they're able to bring a piece with them wherever they go.", 'Guttering cinders stoke their dying flames by snuffing out the lights of others.', "Gyara Spearhurler would have been renowned for her deadly accuracy, if it weren't for her deadly accuracy.", "He didn't hear the cries of the treefolk whose branches he snapped or of the elves caught underfoot. He had eyes only for the path ahead.", 'His blade was forged over coals of moaning treefolk, curved at the optimum angle for severing heads, and heated to volcanic temperatures by his touch.', 'His dreams are filled with noxious powders and clinking vials.', "His sickle was forged in the heat of another cinder's funeral pyre.", "If a spriggan's eyes are larger than its stomach, it has ways to remedy the situation.", 'If even the slightest hint of panic enters the thoughtweft, bakers, potters, and even medics drop their spoons and salves to take up arms.', "If you think you made it past him alive, he's just teasing you.", 'In a world devoid of sun, illumination comes from cheerless fires or the wandering spirits of the dead.', 'In the reflection, she saw the rough shell of the world sloughing away, revealing the truth shining underneath.', 'In the wisps that night, the once timid boggart saw all the terrible, bloody things he was capable of. And it was glorious.', 'In times of portent, the land sculpts itself in accordance with the sigils burned on the sky.', 'It awakened to gloom-fouled skies and responded with a righteous rage that shook the heavens.', 'It gathers hues from the twilight mist so that its master can paint a better world.', 'It harnesses the power of night in a land where daylight fears to show itself.', 'It leaves a trail of crumpled trees and dashed dreams.', 'It scours the hills for living matter, savoring even the tang of poisonous fungi.', 'It shows up at one meal wearing the carcass of the last.', "It wasn't really expected to fly. Then again, it wasn't expected to move, either.", 'It woke to find a vast world in need of a master.', "It's a fool's race to run if all is lost if it be won.", "It's harvest time.", "It's the twisted creation of a kithkin diviner who dreamed of very large crows.", 'Its scars cut deeper than its blade.', "Its victims feel only an itchy, wriggling feeling just under their skin. By then, it's far too late.", 'Kithkin healers chant the clan songs of both their parents over the broth to double its curative effect.', 'Kithkin jealously hoard their knowledge of poultices and remedies so that no outside threat can benefit from their wisdom.', 'Kithkin spellbottlers spend half their time preserving old memories and the other half punishing the new.', 'Knowledge brings the sting of disillusionment, but the pain teaches perspective.', 'Knowledge fills the mind of a fool and opens the mind of the sage.', 'Korrigans, spirits bound to sources of water, shriek when they come upon their own drowned corpses.', 'Made from the clay of burial mounds, the face paint of the priests is a sign of their respect for those whose rest they interrupt.', 'Many have heard the beginning of its low, sustained shriek but few the end.', 'Many horrors take the bait of brave elf volunteers walking alone, only to fall to the blades of rescuers lurking nearby.', 'Merrows skulk the silty bogs around the Wanderbrine, their very thoughts stained with evil.', 'Moonstones grant limited foresight but unlimited advantages.', "Most dirtwalkers only know of the vicious merrows that dwell in the shallows. They can't begin to fathom the wickedness that skulks in the Dark Meanders.", "Most of the Knacksaw clique's skills were hewn from the minds of others.", 'Most such relics remain clasped shut for fear of what ominous truths might be carved into the diptych inside.', 'Mounted cinders circle the blasted peak at Kulrath, hunting the Extinguisher.', "Night after night, Rosheen babbled about a bygone sunlit world, her every word dismissed as a madwoman's ravings.", "No one can navigate the dank maze of Shadowmoor's rivers better than the cruel and covetous merrows. They use the currents to steal—and to steal away.", 'Not all coals lie quietly in their beds of cold ash.', 'Nothing satisfies a merrow as much as drowning what it cannot have.', "Occupancy of the den changes from night to night as boggart gangs fight for control of a place they aren't willing to simply eat.", 'Olka collected the evening mist for years, studying its secrets. Once she learned its essence, she could vanish with a thought.', 'Once a tool of kithkin farmers, scarecrows of all shapes now skitter and lurch across Shadowmoor, animated by residual rustic magics.', 'One head senses the curse. The second loosens it from the soul. The third drinks it as an invigorating mist.', 'One night Oona bottled the sky. The next night she aligned the stars and released it.', 'Ordinary moths follow it, drawn to its light.', 'Parapet watchers patrol the outer edges of the doun, signaling to others who wait patiently in shadow.', 'Scarecrows deemed too malevolent to roam free are shackled to boulders or dolmen stones. Their animosity usually outlives the chains.', 'Seven wives made seven pies from seven apples, each plucked from its branches. Now bare and bitter, it comes to exact its price: one apple, one bone.', "Shadowmoor's main crops are rot, slime, and despair.", 'She whispered a prayer for strength, and her wishes wafted away like seeds on the wind.', "Some don't know his face, but his pets are a dead giveaway.", 'Some elves battled too long in the deep shadow, their swords dipped too often in tainted flesh and poisoned blood.', "Some things aren't worth waiting for.", 'Some words are too important to trust to something as fragile as memory.', "Strategies don't come easily to the boggarts' feral minds, but full-on assault hasn't failed them yet.", 'Stripped of his sight, he was free to see only the ideal.', 'The Aurora is not the only magic capable of remaking a world.', "The Aurora transformed Nibb and Gyik from mischief-makers into feral marauders. They still don't know much about tool safety.", 'The Scuzzback gang scavenges rusty armor covered in barbed protrusions. No threat is more effective than the threat of infection.', 'The Tattermunge gang has no words for the spell that whips their instinctual rage into a frenzy. They only know they like it.', "The boar leads its rider to victory in battle, but it doesn't know how close it is to becoming the victory feast.", 'The cinders believe their flame was stolen by one they call the Extinguisher. All who now wield fire draw their desperate wrath.', 'The dead serve as their own tombstones.', 'The elves alone preserve the few shreds of beauty left. There is no one else who cares.', 'The elves of Wilt-Leaf Wood continually expand the palisade surrounding the sanctuary. They hope to one day enclose the entire forest within its walls.', 'The gate of every kithkin doun is a cunning trap, intended to spill visitors into an oubliette from which there is no escape.', "The giant Tarvik dreamed that trinkets and machines caused all the world's woe. When he awoke from his troubled sleep, he took the name Tarvik Relicsmasher.", "The giant's real punishment was the fleeting moment when he was allowed to stand before being dragged down to his knees again.", 'The kithkin mind-bond is even tighter in Shadowmoor, reinforcing the unity of their community to the point of xenophobia.', 'The last survivor of her patrol, the warrior returned expecting disappointment and scorn. Instead she found gratitude. "You are alive. That is reason to celebrate."', 'The line between dream and death is gauzy and fragile. She leads those too near it from one side to the other.', 'The merrow took a moment for herself. She never gave it back.', "The merrows' prey have retreated from the shore, so they have learned to follow.", "The mission of the Nighthearth, Illulia's cult of murderous cinders, is to intensify every pain suffered in Shadowmoor.", 'The more deadly the lake monster, the shorter the tale.', "The murderous horrors of Raven's Run are legendary, but even that haunted place goes quiet when the night wolves howl.", 'The murk of the Wanderbrine concealed unseemly rituals designed to bring out the worst in merrowkind.', 'The mystic bond between spellcasters and the land is just as vulnerable to attack as the casters themselves.', 'The nova glyph is a potent symbol. A shield embossed with it can resist the force of even the most determined giant.', 'The rivers can no longer provide safe passage for travelers and commerce. They serve only as highways for raiders and channels for blood and woe.', 'The stench of bloodcap mushrooms on the breath is enough to ward off even the most potent magics, especially when combined with a special chant: "Hushhh."', 'The suspicious kithkin of Kinscaer patrol the skies, their eyes attuned to the shapes of outsiders.', 'The thoughtweft is his informant, and he its devoted guardian.', 'The whispers are incomprehensible, yet cinders always hear a message of urgency.', 'The wings are held in place by wicker rods. The rods are held in place by pure faith.', 'Their home uprooted by a giant, the gang of boggarts mourned their old stomping ground.', 'There are things beneath the murk for whom the bog is a stew, a thin broth in need of meat.', 'They envy the life-giving heat so much that they tear it from those who still possess it.', 'They spawn from shadow, wreaking chaos until shadow claims them again.', 'Thick smoke billows and twists to form disturbing faces that cackle and click their teeth to the popping embers.', 'Things of beauty are in constant peril. The riders whisk them to safety, ahead of the encroaching darkness.', 'Those who displease Oona soon learn the extent of the armies she commands.', 'Those who hear her go mad with inspiration.', 'Though the shaman rarely got what she wanted, she was never disappointed in the result.', 'Thoughtweft gives new meaning to the phrase "common knowledge."', 'To reach the ravine of the Wanderbrine River, they were told to take the shortcut "through the mountains." They took the directions literally.', "Untouched by the Aurora, Oona's faeries greeted the night like any other day.", 'Vengeance in stampede form.', 'Vengeance is a dish best served twice.', 'Warrik Brutehexer felt betrayed that his aura favored the depths of the Wanderbrine River over its rightful place, hovering around him.', 'Wells that provide clean, unhaunted water are rare enough to be worth building an entire town around.', 'What the vigor of life builds up, agony tears down again.', 'When elves find a fount of beauty, they protect it. Where there is beauty, there is hope.', 'When giants find their mountain homes infested, they have a whole range of solutions.', 'When gloomwidows mature, they abandon venom in favor of massive webs that span the eaves of cliffs.', 'When night fell, the plane itself was scarred.', 'When the giant Tollek Worldslayer fell, a corruption erupted from his corpse to carry on his name.', 'Whole again in honor and horn.', 'Witches tempted by the power of flame gathered to study in the ruins of Spinerock Knoll.', 'Without the care of the tideshapers, the Lanes lie neglected. Some have flooded entire towns; others dried to cracked mud.', 'Wort had a raiding-bellow that could shatter steel, melt auras, and slice countermagic in half.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Carl Frank', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave DeVries', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dave Kendall', 'Drew Tucker', 'E. M. Gist', 'Eric Fortune', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Ian Edward Ameling', 'Izzy', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Enecio', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry MacDougall', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucio Parrillo', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Nils Hamm', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Pete Venters', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Sardinha', 'Richard Whitters', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Brown', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Altmann', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Terese Nielsen & Ron Spencer', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', "William O'Connor", 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
